# What EAS Build is allowed to upload.
#
# EAS archives from the GIT REPOSITORY ROOT, not from officer_app/ — that is
# its monorepo support, and this repo holds three apps. Without this file it
# falls back to .gitignore, which correctly excludes venv/ (1.4 GB),
# lookout_backend/media/ (3.4 GB) and node_modules/ — but says nothing about
# .git, because nothing ever gitignores its own repository. That directory is
# 451 MB here (the tracked .pt weights have a long history), so every build
# was uploading 451 MB of git history plus 54 MB of source: a 506 MB tarball,
# of which the build needs about 2 MB. On a home connection that upload does
# not reliably finish — it fails with ECONNRESET part-way through.
#
# NOTE: .easignore REPLACES .gitignore for EAS. Anything that must stay out
# has to be named here, even if .gitignore already covers it.

# Ignore everything at the top level...
/*

# ...except the one app EAS actually builds. Its eas.json, app.json and
# package.json all live in here, and it imports nothing from outside it.
!/officer_app

# Inside it, drop what the build either regenerates or installs itself.
officer_app/node_modules/
officer_app/dist/
officer_app/web-build/
officer_app/.expo/
officer_app/android/
officer_app/ios/

# Local-only files that would otherwise ride along.
officer_app/.env
officer_app/expo-qr.png
**/__pycache__/
**/*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
